      en: ["The first Catholic mission was founded in Gondokoro in 1852 by Ignaz Knoblecher.", "Samuel Baker officially annexed the site for Egypt on May 26, 1871.", "The name 'Gondokoro' originates from the Bari language and means 'hill'.", "In 1863, Speke and Grant met Baker here after their discovery of Lake Victoria.", "The post was abandoned in 1874 due to rampant malaria and dysentery.", "Gondokoro was at one time the most important market for ebony and ivory in East Africa."],
